        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(github-copilot): add native web search for Copilot GPT models",
        "body": "Closes #78573\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nGitHub Copilot Responses models support hosted web search, but OpenClaw only exposes the managed `web_search` path for this provider. Users otherwise need another search provider even when their Copilot subscription includes search.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUse Copilot's native Responses `web_search` tool when search is enabled and no managed provider is pinned. This is limited to OpenAI-family Copilot models and still respects `web_search` and `group:web` policy denies.\n\nDirect OpenAI and core orchestration are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCopilot Responses users get hosted search without configuring another provider. Selecting a managed provider such as `brave`, or disabling web search, keeps the existing behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head `54865ec11f` was verified without starting OpenClaw. Running the real provider wrapper against a captured outbound payload produced:\n\n```text\nallowed       tools=[{\"type\":\"web_search\"}] reasoning={\"effort\":\"low\"}\npolicy denied tools=[{\"type\":\"function\",\"name\":\"web_search\"}] reasoning={\"effort\":\"minimal\"}\nbrave pinned  tools=[{\"type\":\"function\",\"name\":\"web_search\"}] reasoning={\"effort\":\"minimal\"}\ngoldeneye     tools=[{\"type\":\"function\",\"name\":\"web_search\"}] reasoning={\"effort\":\"minimal\"}\n```\n\nFocused tests passed: 4 files, 194 tests. Extension production/test type checks, lint, import-boundary checks, docs checks, full build, and the exact-head GitHub CI run passed.\n\nEarlier live Copilot backend proof also returned a completed `web_search_call` with a `url_citation`. The refreshed head was not run through a local Gateway, so final citation rendering was not retested.\n",
